  "id": "COMPOUND:22685 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Resibufagin is implicated in the inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple independent pathways, all of which target the COLO-829 cell line. The evidence suggests that Resibufagin acts as a target for several compounds, including (10'z,13'z)-5-(Nonadeca-1'',13'-Dienyl)Resorcinol, Deoxyaconitine, 3-, and 6alpha-Hydroxycleroda-3,13-dien-16,15-olid-18-oic acid, all of which are known to interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of phosphodiesterase activity, which is a well-documented target for therapeutic interventions. The consistent involvement of COLO-829 in these interactions suggests a possible role in the cellular response to these compounds. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Resibufagin and Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
